        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/30/apple-tv-is-currently-down-for-some-users-as-other-apple-services-also-face-issues/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2024/06/apple-hacked.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Update, September 30, 7:37 p.m. ET: </strong>Apple says all of the outages have now been resolved, with the exception of Apple TV.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Update, October 1, 8:00 p.m. ET: </strong>Apple says the Apple TV issue has finally been resolved.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple is currently reporting issues affecting Apple TV and subscription purchases, while some users are also running into problems elsewhere across the company’s services. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1072187\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/30/apple-tv-is-currently-down-for-some-users-as-other-apple-services-also-face-issues/#more-1072187\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
